From 778d07d20c4a1e69dd212d1de24fa870414e81c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 13:48:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] Add the Program Status Protocol (OSC 7501)

A program reports what it is doing (idle, working, blocked on the user,
done, or failed) with OSC 7501, and asks whether the terminal supports it
with the body "?". Claude Code 2.1.295 and later report this way to any
terminal that answers the query; iTerm2 3.7 implements it.

Konsole now answers the query with the same body, the only bytes the
protocol ever writes back, and parses reports into a ProgramStatusReport,
following the spec's grammar, limits and validation: a malformed pair is
skipped, an unknown state or invalid id ignores the report, and text that
is not valid base64 UTF-8 without control characters, or anything over a
limit, discards it. Reports are emitted as
Emulation::programStatusReported for plugins to keep records and show
them.

Two events the protocol ties records to are now signals too:
Emulation::promptStarted (OSC 133 ; A) and Emulation::terminalReset
(a full reset).

Spec: https://www.superlogical.com/rex/docs/build/program-status

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
